Precision-preserving Qwen4exp decode fusions for exact gfx1151.
The GDN chain derives from halo-box/strix-llama.cpp PR 106 at
9fbe5308fabbc79a53ddee5eadfad74ae0e4710e (MIT), adapted to the current
upstream eight-lane recurrent reduction and explicit input/output lifetimes.
The HC gate fold derives from ggml-org/llama.cpp PR 30602 at
681ae40b5688343dd1a2c6c44b903ba8d5e5ac68 (MIT), integrated into the existing
norm/injection path rather than displacing that larger prefill fusion.

Dispatch retains F32 arithmetic, exact Qwen4exp geometry and conservative
consumer, allocation-lifetime and alias checks. Unsupported graphs fall back.
No weights, KV cache precision, matrix precision or host policy is changed.
The normalization rebase follows upstream's aligned float4 F32 reduction,
with exact positive and misaligned-layout fallback tests.
The scalar softplus expression must also match upstream unary.cu: retain
log1pf(expf(x)) rather than rounding 1 + expf(x) before taking logf.

